{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Public cfDNA/ctDNA sequencing on the 6000 and X is tiny and shows no growing liquid-biopsy research base in GEO.","detail":"Series matching (cfDNA OR ctDNA OR 'cell-free' OR 'circulating tumor DNA'): Q3'24 6000 = 3, X = 1; Q3'25 6000 = 8, X = 2; Q3'26 6000 = 9, X = 0. That is 4, 10 and 9 series out of roughly 1,400–1,900 human 6000+X series per quarter, about 0.5%. The 6000 share (75%, 80%, 100%) is statistically meaningless at this n. Public GEO lags clinical lab work, and clinical labs rarely deposit, so it is a weak proxy for MRD Gb.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=gds&term=GPL24676[ACCN]+AND+gse[ETYP]+AND+(cfDNA+OR+ctDNA+OR+%22cell-free%22+OR+%22circulating+tumor+DNA%22)+AND+2026/07/01:2026/09/30[PDAT]&retmax=0","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI GEO E-utilities","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"No known item counts cfDNA/ctDNA series on these platforms."},
